 "expected_returns": {
  "method": "mean_12m is the expected 12-month log excess return: 12 x the mean monthly log excess return over the asset's whole history through the origin on the return panel (from 1926-07, month-average tier-D eras excluded), identical to the hist_mean benchmark. It is not a model forecast: no model beat it out of sample in the assetpred study or its replication here. se_12m is its standard error from an equal-weighted cosine long-run variance (robust to serial correlation); ci90_lo/ci90_hi is mean_12m +/- t_B(0.95) se_12m with B the number of cosine terms. The interval covers sampling error of the average only, not a mean that has shifted over time. mean_12m_arith = exp(mean_12m + 0.5 cov_annual_ii) - 1 is the arithmetic (simple) 12-month excess return implied by a lognormal with that mean and the published 12-month variance.",
