 "distribution": {
  "method": "Quantile q_k = mean + pscale x Z_k. mean is mean_12m (above); pscale = sqrt(cov_annual_ii + se_12m^2), the published 12-month variance plus the mean's own uncertainty (portfolios: sqrt(w'cov_annual w + (sum|w| se)^2)); Z_k is the shape: quantiles of past standardized outcomes z = (y - mean)/pscale at origins whose 12-month window had closed by the origin, pooled across assets (for portfolios: across the policy portfolios), recentred to mean zero with the spread kept, and with the 1/5/95/99% quantiles floored at a normal of the same standard deviation. 'scale' is sqrt(cov_annual_ii) alone, 'sd' = pscale x sd(Z). Portfolio log returns are approximated by w'r (as in the covariance side's portfolio tests). The distribution model was designed after both holdouts had been seen: its past scores describe it and are not out-of-sample evidence.",
  "model": "dist_hm_af",
  "sensitivity_model": "dist_hm_af.assetshape",
  "tail_floor": [
   "q01",
   "q05",
   "q95",
   "q99"
  ],
  "min_residual_origins": 120,
